5fd6a2b-7bd6-52aa-a601-e8ffdbf177ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-7999" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=7.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =7 \\\\ 7{x}^{2}-{0}^{2} & =7 \\\\ 7{x}^{2} & =7 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $(\\pm 1,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84034/selection/6f65bf5fc685efb73c66e2b8812d2e1b8ac93ae973e09216a37a83512fb94f61" :answer/id #uuid "bc415796-13ef-506a-a175-9a8014f25323" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no $x$-intercepts" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84034/selection/cdd85ece855571ec15906765f821be7e01de0a7fb1476c3bf3705886f38ec5f3" :answer/id #uuid "a2387914-b692-5224-829a-75a8044d4dc0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}},0)-3$ and $(3+\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{5}},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84034/selection/97d0d482cdc3f6e3702eb9dcb9b70c1452afb936e568c7019ece0b60cf9e5206" :answer/id #uuid "b56a848a-b562-50f6-a74d-bc5f43837297" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}},0)$ and $(3+\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{5}},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84034/selection/4b48782c5f994355682d5fafa27873151dd6cb6c7b721f1e79927da43f3e59bb" :answer/id #uuid "8141732a-89ee-55f6-9fd7-8eb64fe35ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{5}},0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84034/selection/a4aea4b5e297f90c9bece2c214af0429837c2183cb91eccfd5e0086f5ec501ed" :answer/id #uuid "a82a4f97-76f1-5905-abca-58d805f2a6bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{5}},0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84034/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69dfec48-55b3-5ce6-afe8-0ca479798c17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84034/selection/6f65bf5fc685efb73c66e2b8812d2e1b8ac93ae973e09216a37a83512fb94f61" :answer-field/choices ["q-84034/selection/6f65bf5fc685efb73c66e2b8812d2e1b8ac93ae973e09216a37a83512fb94f61" "q-84034/selection/cdd85ece855571ec15906765f821be7e01de0a7fb1476c3bf3705886f38ec5f3" "q-84034/selection/97d0d482cdc3f6e3702eb9dcb9b70c1452afb936e568c7019ece0b60cf9e5206" "q-84034/selection/4b48782c5f994355682d5fafa27873151dd6cb6c7b721f1e79927da43f3e59bb" "q-84034/selection/a4aea4b5e297f90c9bece2c214af0429837c2183cb91eccfd5e0086f5ec501ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84034" :question/id #uuid "95b8b9a1-4a35-54df-becb-a839929aef00" :question/math-academy-id "q-84034" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{7}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{7} & =1-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{7} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =-\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions.\nSo, there are no $x$-intercepts." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84034/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-