ersects the line $y=x.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10485/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10485"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278379/field-1/25a170deff842212ed37326913af9f79324c30fcf28877ae81d5293be7b7c870" :answer/id #uuid "7f554c7b-d17f-5c77-afd4-c426d4db0197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278379/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "3516f67c-8400-57dd-8950-fbdc2cfd4afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278379/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebca99b6-0b41-5d45-b988-44e7e1caa00c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278379/field-1/25a170deff842212ed37326913af9f79324c30fcf28877ae81d5293be7b7c870" :answer-field/choices ["q-278379/field-1/25a170deff842212ed37326913af9f79324c30fcf28877ae81d5293be7b7c870" "q-278379/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278379/field-2/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "57cd5bb8-ae05-5714-ac8f-115b1dc1cbf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278379/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a78c9f-93cf-5ed6-a0ae-478cf45b1fae" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278379/field-2/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer-field/choices ["q-278379/field-2/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278379" :question/id #uuid "9241a770-b44b-526b-8e06-9d9a9d471772" :question/math-academy-id "q-278379" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=20$ intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x,$ we first replace $y$ with $\\sqrt{5}x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-\\sqrt{5}$ and $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278379/field-1" "q-278379/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278379"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278380/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "c1be411f-8f3c-5b56-97db-ddbcb3b9fc92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278380/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8836543-2e2d-5065-9b7f-2453e70aa4ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278380/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-278380/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278380/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "34e1d10b-0c86-5712-86fe-ff894c8fbf97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278380/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5990432f-7597-517f-8b75-9782d9feb668" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278380/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-278380/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278380" :question/id #uuid "6bf4a691-ca7d-5cc3-939d-46ca38a01290" :question/math-academy-id "q-278380" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-{y}^{2}=1$ intersects the line $y=\\frac{x}{4}$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\frac{x}{4},$ we first replace $y$ with $\\frac{x}{4}$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-4$ and $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278380/field-1" "q-278380/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278380"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5361"] :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{10} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{10} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7424"] :question/problem "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7y^2 -5x^2 = 28.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2}-5(0)^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2} & =28 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5362"] :question/problem "Calculate the points where the hyperbola \n$\\dfrac{x^2}{10}-\\dfrac{y^2}{15}=1$\nintersects the line $y=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3,$ we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{9}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{3}{5} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6 & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=-3$ at the points $(\\pm 4, -3).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7425"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/assets/c8d69cebc1c7388bb9bc8ac73152a9b2941156188917ee6b680f6758a3d777de.png)\n\nCalculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y = x.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{2}}{225} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{225}{16} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
